            <div type="translation" source="bib:Kuppusamy+al2010_01">
                <p n="1">In the year Āṅkīraca,<note>Sanskrit Āṅgīrasa = Āṅgirasa.</note> on the 10th day of Vaiyyāci.</p>
                <p n="2-8">The all free document given by <gap reason="lost"/> tavataraiyar, the manager of śrī-Maturāyaca <gap reason="lost"/> ruvar Ayyaṉ to Ceṅkaṇa-c-ceṭṭi, Ēṟaiya-c-ceṭṭi, Ālattuṭṭaiya Nampi and Aṟamvaḷatta Nampi, the <foreign>paṭṭaṇavar</foreign> of Kōṭṭuccēri <supplied reason="subaudible">is as follows</supplied>.</p>
                <p n="9-11">The amount of tax fixed by Ayyaṉ for the Paṭṭaṇa-c-cēri of this village is sixty gold
<supplied reason="subaudible">coins</supplied>.</p>
                <p n="11-18">Since the sea fish and <gap reason="lost"/> are inclusive in this sixty gold <supplied reason="subaudible">coins</supplied> which is accrued in this order from this day onwards, let the <foreign>paṭṭaṇavar</foreign> <supplied reason="explanation">fishermen</supplied> themselves enjoy the benefits including the sea fish in Kōṭṭu-c-cēri.</p>
                <p n="18-20">
                    Anyone who harmed this gift</p>
            </div>
            
            <div type="commentary">
                <p n="20">Incomplete or unfinished inscription.</p>
            </div>
            
